# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_extractor_sfc.py" "SFC GATE: PASS" "Svelte and Vue SFC extractor: script block yields def/imports/calls with correct file-line offsets" "Svelte SFC extractor: tree-sitter-svelte locates the script_element raw_text node; JS/TS content parsed by _walk_ts_tree with line_offset=raw_text.start_point.row so start_line/end_line are 1-based lines in the outer .svelte file. Vue SFC extractor: regex pulls the first script/script-setup block; line_offset counted from newlines before the block. Both delegate to the existing TypeScript/JavaScript parser path. BEFORE: 4441 .svelte files produced 0 defs/imports/calls; 0 .vue files recognized at all. AFTER (sveltejs/svelte): 1246 defs, 1413 imports, 3482 calls from .svelte files. AFTER (element-plus): 1148 defs, 2076 imports, 4670 calls from 1004 .vue files. Vue: tree-sitter-vue has no pip wheel so the regex path is the production path (not a fallback). Never-crash: no script block or malformed SFC yields a bare file node with no structural edges." "SFC gate: .svelte fixture with greet() + import helper + call helper -> def greet at start_line 3 (offset applied), imports edge to ./utils, calls edge to helper. .vue fixture with setup() + import ref + call ref -> def setup at start_line 6 (3-line template offset applied), imports edge to ./reactivity, calls edge to ref. Never-crash: template-only .svelte/.vue and malformed SFC yield bare file nodes only, no raise." 12
